--- a/scripts/accounting/README.md
+++ b/scripts/accounting/README.md
@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@
 # WorkItem Accounting
 
+## AR-108 historical token profiles
+
+`TokenHistory.psm1` adds `tokenHistory` to the existing WorkItem metrics projection. It reuses the accepted native identity deduplication and correlation mask and restricts the new history sums to final own `turn_token_usage` counters. Int64 counters cross this new JSON boundary as decimal strings; the browser sums them with BigInt. Existing `tokenUsage`, lifecycle and other metric outputs retain their contracts.
+
+Each history row exposes task/WorkItem/execution/thread/turn plus nullable `roleId`, `modelId`, `reasoningEffort`, `measurementUTC`, separate `importedAtUTC`, provenance, missing metadata and conflicts. Field authority is preserved through enrichment/merge: exact effective native turn context (30) outranks resolved fresh single-turn thread defaults without overrides (20); recorded role assignment (10) remains available. Requested job model/effort is retained separately as `requestedProfiles`, never used as an effective fallback. Equal-authority contradictions make only the affected field unknown; missing values do not erase evidence. `native_rollout` is not a role. Current TOMLs never relabel history. The internal authority marker is meaningful only inside the existing trusted, identity-bound source path; it does not authenticate arbitrary files.
+
+`measurementUTC` is the final native turn measurement timestamp, including the last final snapshot of a proven completed-turn delta. Explicit Z/offset timestamps normalize to UTC; offsetless timestamps stay unknown. Starter notification receipt is retained in `measurementObservationsUTC`, including legacy receipt records, and never bucketed as consumption time. `importedAtUTC` and `projectionGeneratedAtUTC` are separate. Long turns belong to their final measurement bucket, with no estimated distribution. Existing sources provide final turn totals or completed-turn deltas, not an evidenced exhaustive disjoint intra-turn set with profile/time boundaries. Without that set, intra-turn profile conflict stays unknown and the valid turn total counts once. A future evidenced disjoint set must replace the aggregate, preserve all counters, and remain under the existing native identity; no parallel identity is introduced here.
+
+The importer keeps existing usage files immutable and publishes additive `native-token-profile/v1` `*.profile.json` evidence for the same native identity, with no counters. Stable profile content determines its filename; repeating a profile does not add token measurements or duplicate profile files. The public retention reader captures these sidecars as separate `profile` inputs in the observed bundle and publishes their allowlisted schema, task/thread/turn, profile/time fields, conflicts and authority into the retained AccountingDirectory. Profile inputs cannot establish the caller's original task/WorkItem binding or register final counters; the existing reader attaches them only to an existing native identity and proven task alias. Its accepted counter/retention protocol stays intact.
+
+Ledger and sidecar `metadataSources` retain only structured field/value/source, optional SHA256, known effectiveness basis and field authority. Unknown members are skipped before decoding; no private message content is projected. Values use the profile identifier or explicit-offset timestamp rules. Source references are concrete absolute JSON/JSONL paths, optionally with the existing explicit historical import assignment prefix; hashes require 64 hexadecimal characters. The only retained effectiveness basis is the existing resolved fresh-thread-defaults/no-turn-override statement. Invalid references/hash/basis become null, invalid field/value entries are omitted, and missing provenance remains unknown. Paths/hashes are retained historical references, not copied ACK contents or new authentication. Current TOMLs and requested profiles never replace effective sources.
+
+The existing local `metrics(workItemId)` operation returns additive `tokenHistory.version=1`, `scope`, `records`, `excluded`, `coverage`, a content-derived `projectionRevision` and separate generation time. Existing output contracts and request shape are preserved; no new Bridge operation is necessary. The outer `readWindow` describes sequential source reads, not an atomic snapshot. Scope explicitly names the same-store WorkItem family, observed expected native keys and `expectedSetComplete=false`. The configured AccountingDirectory and only explicit supplied native/job/expected sources are read; no global rollout discovery. Unbound CLI tasks are excluded. Native own deduplication and conflict masks precede all filters; inclusive is never added. Diagnostic/provisional counters stay separately in `diagnosticTokenUsage`, outside sums.
+
+`web/token-history.js`, explicitly served by `Start-LocalWeb.ps1`, uses UTC day/Monday-week/calendar-month buckets and filters `[startUtc,endUtc)`. An inclusive UI end date becomes the following day 00:00Z exclusively. Partial buckets use the actual intersection and label it in tooltip and the time-series table. Unknown-time valid tokens remain in the unlimited table; constrained periods show them outside the period sum. Model/effort multiselect uses OR within a field and AND between fields; empty selection means no series. Legend selection filters table, columns, tooltip and visible measured sum together; excluded known tokens are separately shown. Scope gaps and per-field unknown/conflict counts remain unfiltered and overlapping diagnostics are not added. Empty intervals are gaps, not measured zero; an explicit measured zero is preserved. Cached Input and Reasoning Output remain subsets. Chart series pair IDs/colors stay stable.
+
+The Bridge fetches the full family projection; filters are applied synchronously to that revision using current UI settings, without a filtered-result cache. Pending requests additionally bind the snapshot read epoch so a later polling read cannot adopt an older response solely because the store revision stayed the same. Existing five-second polling invalidates the projection cache, including attribution-only changes. The content revision includes attribution and coverage, not merely the WorkItem revision. Product behavior, visual accessibility and live read-window consistency remain unverified under the content-only evidence rule.
+
+Scope remains the selected WorkItem and explicitly bound descendants in the same store. Unbound originalroot/CLI turns require a supported original-owner connection; no automatic completeness is asserted. Missing executions, native turns, correlation, metadata, measurement and family coverage are visible. Implementation evidence under the current repository rule is content/diff/reference read-back only; it is not a current runtime proof or independent acceptance.
+
 Backend adoption design for #50/#51/#24. All seven files in this directory form one patch set under `scripts/accounting/`. Existing store/schema/ledger remain authoritative. No starter, delegation, role or organization changes are part of adoption.
 
 `Import-RolloutTaskUsage.ps1` retains the existing completed-turn snapshot reader. Native thread+turn identifies a measurement; task IDs are assignments and all proven aliases are retained by the reader. Cumulative turn snapshots contribute their final accumulated delta once, not a sum of snapshots; the session fallback requires a proven baseline and final snapshot. Missing baseline produces an explicit unknown measurement. Cache and reasoning remain subsets. Existing records are never upgraded from unknown/provisional to final by replacement: contradictory reimports fail and retain all existing data. Same canonical identity, binding, measurement and finality are idempotent.
